<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 21.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 21.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to June 21 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week June 15-June 21</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 299,951 tns	 30,775 tns    10.26 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	  94,367 tns	  8,239 tns     8.73 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 132,723 tns	 13,037 tns     9.82 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to June 21</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    41,991,306 tns    4,526,438 tns    10.78 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    40,067,932 tns    4,367,710 tns    10.90 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    40,002,435 tns    4,265,948 tns    10.66 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 14 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 5 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 8 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
